{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774026688,"nonce":"7My0GDaJrEcEzHZTqPv3pTTZeL0=","title":"Inbox redesign: work-queue dispatch model with liveness, continuations, and issue-driven navigation","message":"Umbrella issue for the Mandible inbox redesign. Moving from \"show all open issues\" to a work-queue/dispatch model with agent liveness tracking, continuation lifecycle, and issue-driven navigation.\n\n## Design Summary (from two rounds of independent Opus + Gemini analysis)\n\n### Round 1: Core dispatch model\n\n**State machine**: open → committed → merged (+ abandoned as terminal). No \"claimed\" or \"in-progress\" states — liveness and assignment are derived, not stored.\n\n**Activation**: Two-phase model:\n- Phase 1 (worktree creation): `wt --issue \u003cid\u003e` registers work unit immediately. `.issue` file written to worktree for auto-discovery.\n- Phase 2 (first commit): `agent-commit` auto-discovers issue from `.issue` file, updates heartbeat.\n\n**Resolution**: Auth merge success (exitCode === 0) auto-resolves linked work units.\n\n**Work-unit table**: Joins the three hierarchies (issue tree, branch tree, merge tree) into one reconciliation layer. `parent_branch` derived from `__` naming. `kind` (leaf/integration/solo) derived from children.\n\n**Hierarchy alignment**: Umbrella issues ↔ integration branches ↔ non-leaf merge nodes are the same concept. Currently tracked independently via convention. The work-unit table makes the mapping structural.\n\n### Round 2: Liveness, assignment, activity monitor\n\n**Liveness is an overlay, not a state.** Derived at query time by joining work units → sessions → checkLiveness(). SDK sessions: precise (processing flag). PTY: PID alive. External: JSONL mtime.\n\n**Assignment is sticky with staleness flagging.** Worktree exists = assigned. Agent session dies = still assigned. Stale (no live agent, no recent commits, no continuation) = flagged in UI, not auto-released.\n\n**Activity monitor gaps found**:\n1. `last_active` column exists but never written\n2. SDK `processing` flag not exposed to sessions API\n3. `idle` status type-defined but never set\n4. Discovered sessions lack issue/project links\n5. Discovery is pull-only (no periodic scan)\n6. No Gemini in agent patterns\n\n## Open design questions (Round 3 pending)\n\n### Continuations lifecycle\n- Should continuations be tied to issues? (Acknowledge when issue transitions)\n- Should \"resume from continuation\" spawn an SDK agent in Console?\n- Do continuations stay in inbox, or move to the issue detail view?\n\n### Issue-driven navigation\n- Issues tab should show associated sessions, branches, liveness\n- \"Resume work on this issue\" action: find last session, resume or spawn new agent\n- \"Get an agent working on this\" from inbox continuations\n\n### SDK-first framing\n- First-class: SDK agents inside Mandible (Console tab)\n- Second-class: PTY agents inside Mandible\n- Third-class: External shell agents (discovered via process scan)\n- CLAUDE.md should document this hierarchy\n\n### Continuation acknowledgment\n- Current: manual ack via `mandible inbox ack continuation \u003csession-id\u003e`\n- Proposed: auto-ack when the issue transitions (work unit status change)\n- Or: ack when a new session is spawned for the same issue","files":null}]}